[
  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. Patterns of sheet metal bodies with combine_any (mitcad#1462): t=1, r=1, K=0.4. A 40 x 20 panel patterned along x by 40, three in all, each copy joining the sheet it touches: one sheet of 120 x 20 whose Flat Pattern is its blank. Two flat panels A (x=0..40) and B (x=80..120) patterned together along x by 40: A's copy touches both and joins them at once; the joined plate is flat in A's plane, which the sheet-domain adapter re-derives, so it stays a sheet without a warning. The same with B folded at x=110: the joined body holds B's bend, which A's sheet cannot take, so it is an ordinary solid and the feature says so; B's copy touches nothing and is a sheet of its own."},
